From e29bbe0615f2ebdd772c0f42dd8d9dd461cbc83b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A3 <a3@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:07:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1712/1712] field,battle,misc: use the SDK width types the
 helpers declare

NitroSDK s32/u32 are long on 3DS, so GCC 14 rejects the game int/u32
locals at helpers that take s32*/u32*/int*: TaskManager_GetStatePtr
(u32*), Comm_FindFriendSlot (s32*), MapObjectManager_GetNextObjectWith
FlagFromIndex and TrainerSight_FindPlayer (s32*/int*), PlayerAvatar_
GetCoordsInFront (int*), FrontierSpeciesRecords_UpdateFromStat (u32*),
DWC_GetLastErrorEx (int*), CheckUseHeldItem (u32*), ClockWipe_GetScanline
Span (int*), TextOBJ_GetPosition and PokepicScriptAnim_ReadArg (int*/s32*).
Use the callee exact types under SDK_PORT_3DS (locals and PokepicMotion
fields), or cast at the call site for asm tables and header-owned structs
(defaultFieldEffectRenderers, objectIDs, ArcadeContext.weather). The DS
text is unchanged under #else, and that branch reproduces it byte for byte.

Fixes the 3DS compile of src/{battle/battle_controller_player,
communication_player_state,field_move,launch_application,
map_object_behavior,nintendo_wfc_connect,pokepic_anim,screen_window_wipe,
wifi_connection}.c, src/field/{event_cutscene_celebi,event_cutscene_shaymin,
event_cutscene_sinjoh,fieldmap,map_object_models,scrcmd_pokemon_misc}.c and
src/frontier/{battle_hall_data,frontier_cmd_arcade}.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
